# Lifecycle fixture: evaluator exit

Checked-in input for `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_runner_test.exs`, not a
cookbook. Its first cell leaves an unlinked process and its second cell
kills the evaluating process, so the runner must report the exit and still
reclaim the process.

```elixir
unlinked = spawn(fn -> receive do: (:release -> :ok) end)
send(observer, {:exit_fixture, unlinked})
```

```elixir
Process.exit(self(), :kill)
```
